      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_advdiff_nonuniform_dirichlet",
          "description": "Exact unforced advection-diffusion solution u*(x,t) = e^{2x} + e^{-lambda t} e^{x} sin(pi x) with c = 1, nu = 1/2, lambda = 5.434802200544679, fixed-value walls gL = 1, gR = e^2, on the quadratic-stretch mesh (b=0.4). The steady mode e^{2x} (nonzero walls) and the decaying first Dirichlet eigenfunction e^{-lambda t} e^{x} sin(pi x) (homogeneous walls) each solve u_t = -c u_x + nu u_xx exactly, so u* is exact and the discrete drift is the pure spatial truncation of the two operators -- dominated by the advective central_D1_nonuniform_dirichlet_bc term (the rule under test). The diffusion makes the two-sided fixed-value problem well posed and stable; the decay is parabolic, so boundary truncation stays global O(dx^2) in L2 by supraconvergence. References evaluate at the stretched cell centers xc[i] = (xe(i-1)+xe(i))/2, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.05 assertion bounds the truncation-driven L2 error, which falls at order 2. Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_nonuniform_dirichlet/golden/errors.json.",
